// AUTHORED RESTATEMENT BATCH 001.
//
// Each item's three distractors use three different traps — logic_flip,
// agent_swap, timing_shift — so a user's wrong answers reveal WHICH kind of
// misreading they make, not just that they made one.
//
// STATUS: stage 3 only. Not blind-checked, not shippable.
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Because the company failed to renew its licence, it was barred from bidding for public contracts last year.", "correct_answer": "An expired permit is what kept the firm out of government tenders during the previous twelve months.", "distractors": [{"text": "The company was barred from public contracts, and as a result its licence was not renewed.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Public authorities failed to renew the company's licence, which is why it could not bid.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The company will lose the right to bid for public contracts unless it renews its licence.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The licence lapsed first and the ban followed. The first wrong option reverses that order. The second makes the authorities responsible for the lapse when the company was. The third turns a completed exclusion into a future risk.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Although the museum doubled its opening hours, visitor numbers rose only slightly over the following year.", "correct_answer": "Twice as much access brought in barely more people across the next twelve months.", "distractors": [{"text": "Visitor numbers rose so slightly that the museum decided to double its opening hours.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The museum plans to double its opening hours in the hope of attracting more visitors.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Visitors persuaded the museum to double its opening hours after numbers began to fall.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The extra hours came first and produced almost nothing. The first wrong option makes the weak numbers the reason for extending hours. The second moves the change into the future. The third invents visitors as the cause.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The regulation applies to every vessel over twenty metres, regardless of where the vessel is registered.", "correct_answer": "Ships longer than that measurement fall under the rule no matter which country issued their papers.", "distractors": [{"text": "Vessels are registered according to their length, which determines whether the regulation applies.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Vessels over twenty metres must register the regulation wherever they operate.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "From next year the regulation will begin to apply to vessels over twenty metres.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Length decides whether the rule applies; registration is explicitly irrelevant. The first wrong option makes registration depend on length. The second swaps what registers what. The third makes a current rule a future one.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Sales of the device collapsed once a cheaper rival appeared, despite years of favourable reviews.", "correct_answer": "A less expensive competitor destroyed demand for the product, even though critics had praised it for a long time.", "distractors": [{"text": "Favourable reviews caused a cheaper rival to enter the market and take the device's sales.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Sales of the device are expected to fall if a cheaper rival reaches the market.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Reviewers turned against the device once a cheaper rival appeared, and sales collapsed.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The rival caused the collapse; the good reviews are a concession that failed to prevent it. The first wrong option makes the reviews the cause. The second turns a completed collapse into a forecast. The third makes reviewers change their view, which the source denies.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Unless the council receives objections within thirty days, the planning application will be approved automatically.", "correct_answer": "Silence from the public for a month means the building request goes through without further review.", "distractors": [{"text": "The planning application will be rejected automatically if no objections arrive within thirty days.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The council approved the planning application after thirty days of objections were considered.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "The council must object within thirty days or the applicant may proceed with building.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "No objections means approval. The first wrong option inverts the outcome to rejection. The second reports the approval as already given after objections. The third makes the council the objector rather than the public.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The drug performed well in laboratory tests but showed no benefit when trialled on human patients.", "correct_answer": "Promising results under controlled conditions did not carry over to people.", "distractors": [{"text": "The drug helped human patients even though laboratory tests had suggested it would not.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The drug has performed well in the laboratory and will shortly be tested on patients.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Patients reported no benefit, which led researchers to repeat the laboratory tests.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "It worked in the lab and failed in people. The first wrong option reverses both halves. The second puts the human trial in the future when it has happened. The third makes patient reports cause new lab work, which the source does not say.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Rather than closing the branch entirely, the bank reduced its hours and kept two staff on site.", "correct_answer": "The office stayed open with a smaller team and shorter times instead of shutting altogether.", "distractors": [{"text": "The bank closed the branch entirely rather than reduce its hours.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Two members of staff kept the branch open after the bank decided to close it.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The bank intends to reduce the branch's hours before deciding whether to close it.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The branch stayed open in reduced form. The first wrong option chooses the opposite of the two alternatives. The second makes staff act against a closure decision. The third turns a settled outcome into an undecided plan.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Because the report was published during the holidays, almost no journalists noticed its most serious findings.", "correct_answer": "Timing the release for a quiet period meant the gravest conclusions went largely unreported.", "distractors": [{"text": "Journalists ignored the report, so it was published during the holidays.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The report will be published during the holidays, when few journalists are working.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Journalists published the report during the holidays and overlooked its most serious findings.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Publishing during the holidays is why the findings were missed. The first wrong option makes being ignored the reason for the timing. The second moves publication into the future. The third makes journalists the publishers.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The new rule bans advertising aimed at children, though existing campaigns may continue until December.", "correct_answer": "Marketing directed at young people is now forbidden, but adverts already running have until the end of the year.", "distractors": [{"text": "Existing campaigns must stop immediately, while new advertising aimed at children remains permitted.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "From December the new rule will begin to ban advertising aimed at children.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Advertisers have banned campaigns aimed at children, and the rule allows them until December.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "New adverts are banned now; existing ones get until December. The first wrong option swaps which category is protected. The second makes December the start of the ban rather than the end of the exemption. The third makes advertisers the ones imposing the ban.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Farmers who switched to the new seed reported higher yields, but only in fields with good drainage.", "correct_answer": "The variety produced bigger harvests for growers, though the gain appeared solely where water drained well.", "distractors": [{"text": "Good drainage was the result of switching to the new seed, which raised yields.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Seed producers, rather than farmers, reported the higher yields from the new variety.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Farmers expect higher yields once they switch to the new seed next season.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Drainage is the condition under which the seed helps, not something the seed caused. The first wrong option makes drainage an effect. The second changes who reported the result. The third turns a measured outcome into an expectation.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "The city introduced free transport on weekends, and car use in the centre fell sharply within months.", "correct_answer": "Removing fares at the end of the week quickly cut how much people drove downtown.", "distractors": [{"text": "Car use in the centre fell, which persuaded the city to make weekend transport free.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The city hopes that free weekend transport will eventually reduce car use in the centre.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Drivers made transport free at weekends in order to reduce congestion in the centre.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Free transport came first and driving fell after. The first wrong option reverses cause and effect. The second turns a measured fall into a hope. The third makes drivers set the fares.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Although both machines cost the same to buy, the older model is far more expensive to run.", "correct_answer": "The two devices carry an identical purchase price, but keeping the earlier one working costs much more.", "distractors": [{"text": "The older machine is cheaper to run, although it costs more to buy than the newer one.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The older model will become more expensive to run once the new pricing takes effect.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Buyers of the older machine pay more for it, though both cost the same to operate.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Same purchase price, different running cost. The first wrong option swaps which cost differs. The second makes a present fact conditional on future pricing. The third moves the difference back to the purchase price.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "The committee rejected the proposal twice before finally accepting a version that had barely changed at all.", "correct_answer": "After two refusals the panel approved something almost identical to what it had turned down.", "distractors": [{"text": "The committee accepted the proposal at once and rejected the later revised versions.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The committee is expected to reject the proposal twice before accepting a revised version.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "The person who wrote the proposal rejected the committee's changes twice before agreeing.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Two rejections came first, then acceptance of nearly the same thing. The first wrong option reverses the order of acceptance and rejection. The second makes it a prediction. The third swaps who rejected whom.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Nurses were given the training first, and doctors received the same course several months later.", "correct_answer": "The nursing staff completed the programme well before their medical colleagues were offered it.", "distractors": [{"text": "Because doctors had already taken the course, nurses were trained several months later.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Doctors were trained first, and nurses took the same course months afterwards.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Doctors will receive the training several months after the nurses have finished it.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Nurses went first. The first wrong option makes the doctors' training the reason for the delay. The second swaps which group went first. The third leaves the doctors' training still to come, when the source reports it as done.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The bridge was designed to last a century but required major repairs after only thirty years.", "correct_answer": "Intended to survive a hundred years, the crossing needed serious work in less than a third of that time.", "distractors": [{"text": "The bridge needed repairs after thirty years, so it was redesigned to last a century.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The bridge is expected to need major repairs about thirty years from now.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Engineers who repaired the bridge had designed it to last a hundred years.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The design intention failed well short. The first wrong option makes the repairs the reason for the design. The second puts the repairs in the future. The third claims the repairers were the designers, which the source never says.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Because it rained throughout the festival, organisers offered refunds to anyone who left before the final day.", "correct_answer": "Constant wet weather led the people running the event to pay back those who departed early.", "distractors": [{"text": "Organisers offered refunds, and as a result many people left before the festival's final day.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Organisers will offer refunds if it rains throughout the festival next year.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Festival-goers demanded refunds from the organisers once the rain began.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Rain caused the refunds. The first wrong option makes the refunds cause the early departures. The second turns a past response into a future condition. The third makes attendees demand what organisers in fact offered.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The law passed easily in the lower house but stalled for eighteen months in the senate.", "correct_answer": "One chamber approved the bill without difficulty while the other held it up for a year and a half.", "distractors": [{"text": "The senate passed the law quickly, but the lower house delayed it for eighteen months.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The law is expected to pass the lower house before spending months in the senate.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Senators introduced the law in the lower house, where it stalled for eighteen months.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Easy passage in one chamber, long delay in the other. The first wrong option swaps which chamber did which. The second makes both stages future. The third moves the delay to the wrong chamber and adds an introduction the source never mentions.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "Although she had never studied economics formally, her analysis proved more accurate than the bank's own forecasts.", "correct_answer": "Without any training in the subject she still predicted events better than the institution's professional projections did.", "distractors": [{"text": "Her formal training in economics is what made her analysis better than the bank's.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The bank's economists produced a more accurate forecast than she did, despite her lack of training.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "She is studying economics now and expects her forecasts to improve on the bank's.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "She had no formal training and still did better. The first wrong option credits training she never had. The second swaps who was more accurate. The third makes her accuracy a future hope rather than a demonstrated result.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "The scheme was suspended after auditors found that a quarter of the payments could not be explained.", "correct_answer": "Inspectors identified twenty-five per cent of the transfers as unaccounted for, and the programme was halted.", "distractors": [{"text": "The scheme was suspended, which is why auditors were unable to explain a quarter of the payments.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Auditors will suspend the scheme if they cannot explain a quarter of the payments.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Those running the scheme suspended the auditors after a quarter of payments were questioned.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The audit finding caused the suspension. The first wrong option makes the suspension the reason the payments could not be explained. The second turns it into a condition. The third swaps who suspended whom, which reverses the whole situation.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Even though the software was free, most schools chose the paid alternative because it came with support.", "correct_answer": "Institutions mostly bought the commercial product for its assistance, despite a version costing nothing being available.", "distractors": [{"text": "Schools chose the free software because the paid alternative offered no support.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Software companies gave schools the paid version free of charge, along with support.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Schools will switch to the paid alternative once support for the free version ends.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "Support is why schools paid rather than took the free option. The first wrong option flips which product had support and which was chosen. The second removes the payment entirely. The third turns a completed choice into a future switch.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "Production stopped for six weeks while the factory replaced equipment that had been in use since 1998.", "correct_answer": "The plant halted output for a month and a half to install machinery replacing what had run for decades.", "distractors": [{"text": "The factory replaced its equipment because production had already stopped for six weeks.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The factory will stop production for six weeks in order to replace ageing equipment.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Equipment suppliers halted production at the factory for six weeks while carrying out replacements.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The replacement is why production stopped. The first wrong option makes the stoppage the reason for replacing. The second puts a completed shutdown in the future. The third makes suppliers rather than the factory halt production.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"cefr": "C1", "source_sentence": "The charity spends less on administration than almost any comparable organisation, according to its published accounts.", "correct_answer": "Its own financial statements show that running costs are lower there than at nearly all similar bodies.", "distractors": [{"text": "The charity's published accounts show it spends more on administration than similar organisations.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "An outside auditor, rather than the charity itself, published the comparison of administrative costs.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The charity intends to reduce its administrative spending below that of comparable organisations.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "It already spends less, on its own published figures. The first wrong option reverses the comparison. The second changes who published the accounts. The third makes an existing position into an intention.", "difficulty_est": 5}
{"cefr": "B1", "source_sentence": "Tickets sold out within an hour, although the venue had added two extra performances that morning.", "correct_answer": "Even with a pair of additional shows announced earlier that day, everything was gone in sixty minutes.", "distractors": [{"text": "The venue added two extra performances because tickets had not sold quickly enough.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The venue will add two extra performances if tickets sell out within an hour.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Ticket agents added two extra performances after the venue sold out within an hour.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "Extra shows were added and everything still sold instantly. The first wrong option makes slow sales the reason for adding them. The second makes the additions conditional and future. The third puts the additions after the sell-out and credits agents.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"cefr": "B2", "source_sentence": "The virus spreads easily but causes serious illness in only a small proportion of those infected.", "correct_answer": "Transmission happens readily, though few of the people who catch it become badly unwell.", "distractors": [{"text": "The virus rarely spreads, but almost everyone who catches it becomes seriously ill.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The virus is expected to spread easily once restrictions are lifted next month.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Those infected spread serious illness to a small proportion of the people they meet.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "It spreads widely but rarely does serious harm. The first wrong option inverts both halves. The second turns a current property into a forecast. The third makes the small proportion describe who gets infected rather than who becomes seriously ill.", "difficulty_est": 4}
